      "description": "Fast access to About, Work and Résumé.",
      "html": "<nav class=\"ds-nav\" aria-label=\"Main navigation\"><a class=\"ds-control\" href=\"#about\">About</a><a class=\"ds-control\" href=\"#work\">Work</a><a class=\"ds-control\" href=\"#resume\">Résumé ↗</a></nav>",
      "css": ".ds-nav{display:inline-flex;gap:28px;align-items:center;padding:12px 24px;border-radius:30px;background:#f4f2e8ed;border:1px solid #68754825;color:var(--ink,#2c3928);font:12px/1.7 \"Instrument Sans\",Arial,sans-serif}.ds-nav a{color:inherit;text-decoration:none}.ds-nav a:hover{text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:5px}.ds-control:focus-visible{outline:2px solid #a65d3a;outline-offset:6px}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Collection filters",
      "kind": "chip",
      "refersTo": "collection-filter",
      "description": "Plain text collection selection with a visible active underline.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-filters\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Choose a collection\"><button class=\"ds-control\" aria-pressed=\"true\">The whole garden</button><button class=\"ds-control\" aria-pressed=\"false\">Published case studies</button><button class=\"ds-control\" aria-pressed=\"false\">Garden studies</button></div>",
      "css": ".ds-filters{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:25px;padding-bottom:17px;border-bottom:1px solid #677a4730}.ds-filters button{background:none;border:0;font:11px/1.7 \"Instrument Sans\",Arial,sans-serif;padding:6px 0;color:#5c6951;cursor:pointer}.ds-filters button[aria-pressed=true]{border-bottom:1px solid var(--ink,#2c3928);color:var(--ink,#2c3928)}.ds-filters button:hover{color:var(--ink,#2c3928)}.ds-control:focus-visible{outline:2px solid #a65d3a;outline-offset:6px}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Herbarium label",
      "kind": "card",
      "refersTo": "specimen-label",
      "description": "The paper identification label beneath a botanical project specimen.",
      "html": "<button class=\"ds-control ds-specimen\"><span class=\"ds-name\">CAREY</span><span class=\"ds-type\">Service design</span><span class=\"ds-collection\">Garden study <svg viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M4 16 16 4M5 4h11v11\"/></svg></span></button>",
      "css": ".ds-specimen{display:block;width:265px;position:relative;text-align:left;background:#f7f3e6;padding:18px 20px;border:0;border-top:1px solid #65734328;box-shadow:0 9px 18px #3c4d2710;color:#4d405f;cursor:pointer;transition:transform .7s cubic-bezier(.16,1,.3,1)}.ds-specimen:before{content:\"\";position:absolute;left:50%;top:-10px;width:1px;height:13px;background:#7b8362}.ds-name{display:block;font:30px/1.1 \"Instrument Serif\",Georgia,serif;letter-spacing:-.02em}.ds-type{display:block;font:10px/1.7 \"Instrument Sans\",Arial,sans-serif;margin-top:6px}.ds-collection{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;font:9px/1.7 \"Instrument Sans\",Arial,sans-serif;color:#6e735b;margin-top:18px}.ds-collection svg{width:16px;height:16px;fill:none;stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:1.1}.ds-specimen:hover{transform:translateY(-8px)}.ds-control:focus-visible{outline:2px solid #a65d3a;outline-offset:6px}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Pressed collaborator note",
      "kind": "card",
      "refersTo": "pressed-note",
      "description": "Tactile quiet paper for a real collaborator quotation.",
      "html": "<article class=\"ds-note\"><span class=\"ds-pin\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><blockquote>“Dependable and curious, she brings clarity, care, and great energy to every project.”</blockquote><p><strong>Aastha Lathia</strong><span>Co-worker, IIT Delhi</span></p></article>",
      "css": ".ds-note{position:relative;max-width:290px;min-height:370px;padding:38px 30px 100px;background:#e2dfeb;color:var(--ink,#2c3928);box-shadow:0 12px 25px #4e4f3020;transform:rotate(-4deg)}.ds-note blockquote{margin:0;font:28px/1.2 \"Instrument Serif\",Georgia,serif;letter-spacing:-.01em}.ds-note p{font:11px/1.7 \"Instrument Sans\",Arial,sans-serif;margin:25px 0 0}.ds-note strong{display:block;font-weight:500}.ds-note p span{display:block;font-size:9px;opacity:.85}.ds-pin{position:absolute;width:6px;height:6px;border-radius:50%;background:#756647;top:17px;left:50%;box-shadow:1px 3px 5px #5b542e40}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Diary page control",
      "kind": "button",
      "refersTo": "diary-control",
      "description": "Manual navigation between personal diary spreads.",
      "html": "<button class=\"ds-control ds-diary\">Turn a page <span aria-hidden=\"true\">→</span></button>",
      "css": ".ds-diary{font:11px/1.7 \"Instrument Sans\",Arial,sans-serif;padding:5px 9px;border:0;background:#f4f2e8ba;border-radius:20px;color:var(--ink,#2c3928);cursor:pointer}.ds-diary span{margin-left:12px}.ds-diary:hover{background:var(--paper,#f4f2e8)}.ds-control:focus-visible{outline:2px solid #a65d3a;outline-offset:6px}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "A Polymath's Garden",
    "overview": "A personal botanical world where scroll is time and time is growth. Warm paper, olive ink, family photographs, dithered plants and quiet editorial type make the portfolio feel like a diary discovered inside a garden. Nature provides the setting: leaves overhead, roots below, flowers and grass in the foreground, then a green hill under blue sky and clouds.\n\nThe garden moves through seed arrival, canopy diary, underground roots, herbarium work, pressed collaborator notes, an experimental greenhouse and the hills beyond. Continuous dawn-to-noon atmosphere and warm late-afternoon landscape light hold the scenes together. Hiring teams can skip directly to Work; fixed navigation and the growing vine keep the story navigable. The Orto Botanico di Padova inspiration remains explicit. Asset provenance belongs in ASSETS.md and factual claims remain grounded in PRODUCT.md.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Warm personal diary with real family photographs.",
      "Quiet Instrument Serif and Instrument Sans editorial hierarchy.",
      "ASCII, sampled pigment, dithered botanical collage, pixel planting and shader light.",
      "A continuous natural environment with scroll-linked growth.",
      "Direct Work access, keyboard navigation, lighter mobile scenes and readable motion-off flow."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Paper and Plant Rule",
        "body": "Keep botanical color in the framing and emphasis; preserve quiet reading surfaces around body copy and case-study artwork.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Two Voices Rule",
        "body": "Use serif for expressive narrative and sans-serif for reading, controls, attribution, and metadata.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Quiet Depth Rule",
        "body": "Let collage, overlap, and tonal fields establish hierarchy before adding shadows.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** preserve the garden world, warm paper, botanical greens and expressive serif/sans pairing.",
      "**Do** use real family photographs and case-study artwork with provenance recorded in ASSETS.md.",
      "**Do** retain fixed navigation, direct Work anchors and the published-case-study filter.",
      "**Do** preserve all reading content and functional controls when motion is paused or reduced.",
      "**Do** label supplied garden studies and original browser experiments honestly."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** turn the garden into unrelated panels with disconnected entrance effects.",
      "**Don't** obscure copy with plants, textures or animated layers.",
      "**Don't** carry desktop sticky scenes, botanical canvas resolution or animated shader rendering into the mobile layout.",
      "**Don't** invent project outcomes, endorsements or process detail.",
      "**Don't** require animation, hovering or a long scroll to reach the published work."
    ]
  }
}
